  "worked_solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third equations we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1} & =-6 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =8 \\\\ 4(-1)+3{x}_{2} & =8 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} & =12 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & =-11 \\\\ 3(-1)-2(4) & =-11 \\\\ -11 & =-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ which means\n\n$$\n-{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+4=3.\n$$",
